{
  "comment": "Shared contract for the CAD selector grammar. The Python parser (cadgen.cad_ref_syntax) and the JS parser (@text-to-cad/core/lib/cadRefs.js) are separate implementations of the same language; this fixture is the only thing that keeps them honest. Every case must hold in BOTH. A ref names geometry: an occurrence token (`o:` + 12 hex) and an element name under an occurrence token or a part label, joined by `/`. An element name is its kind (`f:`/`e:`/`v:`) and its lineage -- a feature (a label, or `function.operationN`), the element's number among what that feature made and, for a piece of a split element, the piece's number -- or, for an element no construction names, its geometric token (12 hex). Cases tagged phase 1 cover label selectors.",
